:"a5ab3d0b81c3595a","content":"1fdc579b816bd18b"},"doc":"**LLN for the assignment martingale.** For a `[0,1]`-valued adapted\nintegrable assignment indicator `X` on a probability space, the assignment martingale `M` satisfies\n`M n / n → 0` almost everywhere. The increments are bounded by `1`, so the martingale strong law of\nlarge numbers `martingale_div_atTop_ae_tendsto_zero_of_bdd` applies. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1"},{"explicit":false,"name":"m0","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"μ","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"ℱ","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Filtration ℕ m0"},{"explicit":false,"name":"X","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → ℝ"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ"},{"explicit":true,"name":"hX","role":"hypothesis","type":"MeasureTheory.StronglyAdapted ℱ X"},{"explicit":true,"name":"hX_int","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ (n : ℕ), MeasureTheory.Integrable (X n) μ"},{"explicit":true,"name":"h0X","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ (n : ℕ), 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] X n"},{"explicit":true,"name":"h1X","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ (n : ℕ), X n ≤ᵐ[μ] fun x => 1"}],"conclusion":"∀ᵐ (ω : Ω) ∂μ, Filter.Tendsto (fun n => assignMart X ℱ μ n ω / ↑n) Filter.atTop (nhds 0)","decl":"AlphaRAR.assignMart_div_atTop_ae_tendsto_zero"},"code":"/-- **LLN for the assignment martingale.** For a `[0,1]`-valued adapted\nintegrable assignment indicator `X` on a probability space, the assignment martingale `M` satisfies\n`M n / n → 0` almost everywhere. The increments are bounded by `1`, so the martingale strong law of\nlarge numbers `martingale_div_atTop_ae_tendsto_zero_of_bdd` applies. -/\nlemma assignMart_div_atTop_ae_tendsto_zero [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n    (hX : StronglyAdapted ℱ X) (hX_int : ∀ n, Integrable (X n) μ)\n    (h0X : ∀ n, 0 ≤ᵐ[μ] X n) (h1X : ∀ n, X n ≤ᵐ[μ] fun _ ↦ (1 : ℝ)) :\n    ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, Tendsto (fun n ↦ assignMart X ℱ μ n ω / n) atTop (𝓝 0)","proof":":= by\n  have hΔ k : ∀ᵐ ω ∂μ, |assignMart X ℱ μ (k + 1) ω - assignMart X ℱ μ k ω| ≤ 1 := by\n    filter_upwards [abs_assignMart_succ_sub_le hX_int h0X h1X k] with ω h\n    simpa only [Pi.sub_apply] using h\n  exact martingale_div_atTop_ae_tendsto_zero_of_bdd (martingale_assignMart hX hX_int) hΔ","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/YDK2026/AssignmentRate.lean","start":51,"end":62,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/YDK2026/AssignmentRate.lean#L51-L62"},"deps":[455],"outside":[],"external":[["AddCommMonoid","mathlib","class"],["Bot.bot","mathlib","definition"],["BoundedOrder.toOrderBot","mathlib","instance"],["CompleteLattice.toBoundedOrder","mathlib","instance"],["CompleteLattice.toLattice","mathlib","instance"],["DivInvMonoid.toDiv","mathlib","instance"],["Filter.Eventually","mathlib","definition"],["Filter.EventuallyLE","mathlib","definition"],["Filter.Tendsto","mathlib","definition"],["Filter.atTop","mathlib","definition"],["Finset.range","mathlib","definition"],["Finset.sum","mathlib","definition"],["HDiv.hDiv","lean4","definition"],["InnerProductSpace.toNormedSpace","mathlib","instance"],["Lattice.toSemilatticeSup","mathlib","instance"],["MeasurableSpace","mathlib","class"],["MeasurableSpace.instCompleteLattice","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration.mk","mathlib","constructor"],["MeasureTheory.Filtration.seq","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.Integrable","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure","mathlib","class"],["MeasureTheory.Measure","mathlib","structure"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.instFunLike","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.Measure.instOuterMeasureClass","mathlib","instance"],["MeasureTheory.StronglyAdapted","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.ae","mathlib","definition"],["MeasureTheory.martingalePart","mathlib","definition"],["Nat","lean4